# Shalean Engineering Standard

Read and follow `AGENTS.md`, `docs/engineering/SHALEAN_ENGINEERING_STANDARD.md`, and the current release-control standard before changing code.

## Workflow

- Work on the approved feature, fix, chore, docs or audit branch; never develop directly on `main` or `staging`.
- Keep the requested scope together and avoid unrelated refactors.
- If an old branch is badly stale, do not force-merge it over newer production controls; salvage still-valid changes onto current `main`.
- Run the relevant local tests and rely on required GitHub checks for merge readiness.
- Use staging when runtime acceptance is required; docs/governance-only work normally does not require staging.
- Merge to `main` only after explicit authorization and green required checks.
- Minimize unnecessary Vercel builds and redeployments.

## Safety

- Server-side authorization is the source of truth.
- Preserve least privilege and fail closed for unknown roles, permissions and scopes.
- Never expose secrets, service-role keys, payment credentials, customer PII, cleaner identity documents or bank details.
- Do not weaken maker-checker, audit, payout, earnings, payment or booking-integrity controls.
- Never edit an applied production migration; create a forward migration.
- Prefer idempotent handling for payments, invoices, recurring bookings, notifications and payouts.
- Use integer cents for monetary logic where the approved domain model supports it.
- Treat `Africa/Johannesburg` as the operational timezone unless an integration explicitly requires UTC.

## Before review

Report the branch, files changed, behaviour implemented, tests and results, security/financial/database impact, environment changes, staging status, risks and remaining verification. Never claim a check or production verification that was not performed.
